<!--ID=5B95B1CC-2C7B-494F-B746-CF22A0E779B7;Version=1|{"Locales":{"en-US":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]},"en-GB":{"AutoApplyCustomLexiconFiles":[{}]}}}-->
<speak xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis"
       xmlns:mstts="http://www.w3.org/2001/mstts"
       xmlns:emo="http://www.w3.org/2009/10/emotionml"
       version="1.0"
       xml:lang="en-GB">
  <voice name="en-GB-OllieMultilingualNeural">
    <prosody rate="-10.50%" pitch="-2.50%">
      In Genesis, we hear of a time when many hearts were restless and harsh.<break time="500ms"/>
      The earth felt loud with violence and sorrow.<break time="500ms"/>
      And God saw it clearly.<break time="1000ms"/>
      Not with surprise, but with steady truth.<break time="1800ms"/>

      In that same world, there was a man named Noah.<break time="500ms"/>
      Noah walked with God.<break time="1000ms"/>
      And Noah found favour.<break time="1800ms"/>

      God spoke to Noah about what was coming.<break time="500ms"/>
      A flood that would cover the land.<break time="500ms"/>
      And God also spoke about a way through.<break time="1000ms"/>
      A shelter.<break time="1800ms"/>

      Noah listened.<break time="500ms"/>
      He received the word.<break time="500ms"/>
      And he kept walking, one step at a time.<break time="1800ms"/>

      God sees what is real.<break time="1000ms"/>
      God makes a way to carry life.<break time="1000ms"/>
      You are safe in God's care.<break time="1800ms"/>
      You can rest.<break time="3800ms"/>
    </prosody>
  </voice>
</speak>
